.TH "CSSKEYWORDVALUE.CSSKEYWORDVALUE" "3JS" "August 29, 2026" "JavaScript" "JavaScript Reference Manual"
.SH NAME
CSSKeywordValue.CSSKeywordValue \- CSSKeywordValue: CSSKeywordValue()
constructor
.SH SYNOPSIS
\f[B]Note:\f[R] This feature is available in Web Workers.
.PP
The \f[B]\f[CB]CSSKeywordValue()\f[B]\f[R] constructor creates a new
\f[CR]CSSKeywordValue\f[R] object which represents a CSS keyword or
other identifier.
.SH SYNTAX
.IP
.EX
new CSSKeywordValue(value)
.EE
.SS Parameters
.TP
\f[B]value\f[R]
A \f[CR]String\f[R] that will be used to set
\f[CR]CSSKeywordValue.value\f[R].
.SS Exceptions
.TP
\f[B]TypeError\f[R]
Thrown if the \f[CR]value\f[R] parameter is not specified, or if it is
an empty string.
.SH EXAMPLES
.SS Basic usage
This example sets the CSS \f[CR]display\f[R] property to
\f[CR]initial\f[R], constructing a \f[CR]CSSKeywordValue\f[R] for the
keyword.
.SS HTML
The HTML defines an element on which we\(cqll set the value of the
\f[CR]display\f[R] keyword, an \f[CR]<hr>\f[R] element, a button that
will be used to set the value of the \f[CR]display\f[R] keyword, and a
\(lqReset\(rq button to reset the example.
.IP
.EX
<\f[B]div\f[R] id=\(dqmyElement\(dq>
  Check the developer tools to see the log in the console and to inspect this
  div\(aqs style attributes.
</\f[B]div\f[R]>
<\f[B]hr\f[R] />
<\f[B]button\f[R] id=\(dqset\-initial\(dq type=\(dqbutton\(dq>Set initial</\f[B]button\f[R]>
<\f[B]button\f[R] id=\(dqreset\(dq type=\(dqbutton\(dq>Reset</\f[B]button\f[R]>
.EE
.SS CSS
The CSS initially sets the element to \f[CR]flex\f[R], which forces it
to display full\-width, and gives it a solid border with padding and
margins.
.IP
.EX
myElement {
  \f[B]display\f[R]: flex;
  \f[B]border\f[R]: solid;
  \f[B]padding\f[R]: 10px;
  \f[B]margin\f[R]: 5px;
}
.EE
.SS JavaScript
The code first gets a handle to the \(lqSet initial\(rq button and adds
a listener to handle the click event when it is pressed.
.PP
The listener then gets the element\(cqs inline styles using
\f[CR]HTMLElement.attributeStyleMap\f[R], and sets the
\f[CR]display\f[R] attribute with a newly constructed
\f[CR]CSSKeywordValue\f[R].
It then logs the value of that keyword to the console.
.IP
.EX
\f[B]const\f[R] setInitialButton = document.querySelector(\(dq#set\-initial\(dq);

setInitialButton.addEventListener(\(dqclick\(dq, () \f[B]=>\f[R] {
  \f[B]const\f[R] myElementInlineStyles =
    document.getElementById(\(dqmyElement\(dq).attributeStyleMap;
  myElementInlineStyles.set(\(dqdisplay\(dq, \f[B]new\f[R] CSSKeywordValue(\(dqinitial\(dq));
  console.log(\(gadisplay: ${myElementInlineStyles.get(\(dqdisplay\(dq).value}\(ga);
});
.EE
.PP
Note that we can\(cqt log the value of the inline styles before pressing
the button, because there aren\(cqt any.
.SS Result
Right click on the element and open the \c
.UR https://firefox-source-docs.mozilla.org/devtools-user/page_inspector/how_to/select_an_element/index.html
developer tools inspector
.UE \c
\ to inspect its styles.
You should see that \f[CR]display: flex\f[R] is set on
\f[CR]#myElement\f[R].
Press \(lqSet initial\(rq to make set the inline style of
\f[CR]display\f[R] to \f[CR]\(dqinitial\(dq\f[R].
You should see the styles change in the inspector, and the element will
also shrink slightly as the \f[CR]flex\f[R] is disabled.
